WEBVTT


00:02:40.272 --> 00:02:42.556
Cody!


00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.874
Just the man I wanted to see.


00:02:45.945 --> 00:02:49.136
Zack. Just the man I want
to see walking away.


00:02:49.207 --> 00:02:52.468
Now, normally I'd be insulted by that,


00:02:52.536 --> 00:02:54.981
But I need to talk to you,


00:02:55.047 --> 00:02:57.244
So I'll return just the insult later.


00:02:57.319 --> 00:02:59.471
But just know, it's gonna
be about that shirt.


00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.378
Look, Zack, now's not a good time.


00:03:01.441 --> 00:03:03.355
You still haven't told
Bailey yet, have you?


00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:04.498
Why are you so scared to tell Bailey.


00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.126
You're doing an internship
over spring break?


00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.902
Because, you know, we've made
special plans for the week,


00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:12.786
And this is also the last spring
break before our graduation.


00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.256
She cannot take me.


00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.886
She put you in a headlock with her thumb.


00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:18.506
You blacked out.
You missed November.


00:03:18.578 --> 00:03:20.300
They had to re-inflate your
lungs with a bicycle pump.


00:03:20.362 --> 00:03:23.006
Okay, maybe she can take me.


00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.699
Which is why I wrote
everything in this letter.


00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.466
She'll understand when she reads it,


00:03:27.526 --> 00:03:29.020
And I'll be nowhere near when she does.


00:03:29.092 --> 00:03:31.086
Cody, I've got good news.


00:03:31.157 --> 00:03:33.152
You're a hologram and I'm an only child?


00:03:33.221 --> 00:03:36.484
Better. I think I can help you
with this pesky Bailey situation.


00:03:36.553 --> 00:03:40.014
Then think again, unless the
first time exhausted you.


00:03:40.075 --> 00:03:41.411
Good one.


00:03:43.336 --> 00:03:44.332
Sorry.
Out!


00:03:45.101 --> 00:03:46.099
Come on.


00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:52.420
Okay, so, here's my proposal.


00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:54.218
Let me break the news to Bailey,


00:03:54.287 --> 00:03:56.920
Therefore, giving her time to break
other things rather than your bones,


00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.483
And in return, you give me the car.


00:03:59.545 --> 00:04:01.011
What car?


00:04:01.081 --> 00:04:03.105
Dad's vintage sports car,
that he and mom promised you.


00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.099
For getting into college.


00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.864
Which is a big building where
people go to learn things.


00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.469
Oh, well, then, maybe they can teach you.


00:04:09.529 --> 00:04:11.624
How to get along without a
car, because I want it.


00:04:11.693 --> 00:04:15.433
Why? The only place you go more
than once a day is the bathroom.


00:04:15.504 --> 00:04:18.264
And how much nicer
would it be to drive there?


00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:20.274
I call shotgun!
Forget it.


00:04:20.335 --> 00:04:23.305
The car is mine, and I certainly
don't need your help with Bailey.


00:04:23.376 --> 00:04:25.004
No, you need me.


00:04:25.075 --> 00:04:27.046
Zack, give that back. Zack!
Hey, come on, let that go!


00:04:27.114 --> 00:04:30.587
Careful with that, Zack.
Give me that. No! No!


00:04:31.856 --> 00:04:33.316
First, it's special delivery.


00:04:34.757 --> 00:04:36.226
And now, it's air mail.


00:04:36.286 --> 00:04:38.985
Guess you're gonna have
to write another letter.


00:04:39.056 --> 00:04:42.027
That took me 14 hours to compose.


00:04:42.095 --> 00:04:43.997
Why is it whenever something
is important to me,


00:04:44.065 --> 00:04:45.766
You always find a way to ruin it?


00:04:46.898 --> 00:04:47.937
It's fun...


00:04:47.997 --> 00:04:50.808
Oh. Now, I have to
explain to Bailey.


00:04:50.866 --> 00:04:54.278
Something I was able to write
so eloquently in sanskrit.


00:04:54.338 --> 00:04:56.178
Go away, Zack.


00:04:56.247 --> 00:04:58.477
I don't want you standing anywhere
near here when I talk to Bailey.


00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:00.719
When you say, "near here..."


00:05:03.888 --> 00:05:04.890
Everywhere!


00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.190
Wow, wow!


00:05:08.258 --> 00:05:10.259
Try and help out your brother
for no other reason.


00:05:10.331 --> 00:05:13.060
Than to get something from him,
and this is the thanks you get?


00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.059
Come, woodster, we're leaving.


00:05:16.128 --> 00:05:17.400
You know, between moseby and Cody,


00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.299
We're not really not welcome
anywhere on this ship.


00:05:19.371 --> 00:05:20.670
Which is weird because we're adorable.


00:05:20.741 --> 00:05:22.301
I know, right?
Quite.


00:05:47.632 --> 00:05:51.102
So, then the neutron asked, "hey, waiter,


00:05:51.174 --> 00:05:54.443
"how much is the soda?
" and the waiter responded with,


00:05:54.503 --> 00:05:55.903
"for you, no charge!"


00:05:55.974 --> 00:06:00.085
oh, this day is perfect.


00:06:00.144 --> 00:06:02.414
Yes, it is. So far.


00:06:02.485 --> 00:06:04.355
Okay, so let's talk about spring break.


00:06:04.414 --> 00:06:07.424
I am so excited.
I've been planning our trip for a month.


00:06:07.484 --> 00:06:09.793
Yeah, well, that's not very thorough.


00:06:09.855 --> 00:06:11.556
Can you believe we're finally going to see.


00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:13.925
The majestic ancient redwoods?


00:06:13.993 --> 00:06:18.165
Oh, uh, did you know that
over 7,000 species.


00:06:18.236 --> 00:06:20.835
Of lethal insects make
colonies in aged wood?


00:06:20.906 --> 00:06:22.865
Duh! Okay, and then,
we're going to watch.


00:06:22.935 --> 00:06:24.635
The Northwestern lemming run,


00:06:24.708 --> 00:06:27.177
Where lemmings instinctively
hurl their furry little bodies.


00:06:27.247 --> 00:06:29.447
Right off of those picturesque cliffs.


00:06:29.516 --> 00:06:33.917
Well, nothing says spring break
like dodging falling rodents.


00:06:33.989 --> 00:06:35.747
Okay. What is going on?


00:06:35.818 --> 00:06:39.057
I've been trying to
tell you this whole time...


00:06:39.129 --> 00:06:41.787
Cody, just the man I wanted to see...


00:06:41.858 --> 00:06:43.229
Zack!


00:06:43.298 --> 00:06:46.499
Look, this is only gonna take a
sec, and I wanna tell you...


00:06:46.568 --> 00:06:50.070
Woody, Woody...
Down. Like I showed you.


00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:51.939
I'm not good with machinery that moves.


00:06:52.007 --> 00:06:54.309
I once fell down an
escalator for over an hour!


00:06:55.038 --> 00:06:57.279
Easy, Woody, easy.


00:06:57.341 --> 00:06:59.781
Zack, what are you doing here?


00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.782
You said not to "stand" anywhere
near you while you talk to Bailey.


00:07:02.849 --> 00:07:05.680
But I'm not standing.
I'm swinging.


00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:08.051
Is this about that car?


00:07:08.121 --> 00:07:11.492
Yes. Mom and dad
promised it to you,


00:07:11.562 --> 00:07:13.492
So they won't let me have it
unless you say it's okay.


00:07:13.562 --> 00:07:16.301
Zack, I'm talking to Bailey right now.
I would really prefer...


00:07:16.361 --> 00:07:18.660
You haven't told her yet?


00:07:18.732 --> 00:07:23.244
Bailey, Cody is going to do an internship
at a biology reserve over spring break.


00:07:23.302 --> 00:07:25.372
Excuse me?


00:07:25.441 --> 00:07:26.513
Cody is what?


00:07:26.572 --> 00:07:27.741
Guess not.


00:07:27.813 --> 00:07:29.514
Wait, our last spring break together,


00:07:29.583 --> 00:07:31.843
And you choose some
biology reserve over me?


00:07:31.912 --> 00:07:35.453
No, Bailey... Okay, yes.


00:07:35.524 --> 00:07:38.053
I've been trying to tell
you, but I couldn't.


00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:40.493
Look, I wrote it all down in a
letter explaining everything,


00:07:40.554 --> 00:07:42.053
But Zack lost it.


00:07:42.125 --> 00:07:44.464
A letter?
You put this in a letter?


00:07:44.524 --> 00:07:45.594
Can you believe that?


00:07:47.095 --> 00:07:49.035
You let me go on and on, talking about.


00:07:49.105 --> 00:07:50.735
How much this spring break meant to me,


00:07:50.805 --> 00:07:52.565
When the whole time, you made other plans.


00:07:52.636 --> 00:07:53.674
I know.


00:07:53.735 --> 00:07:56.643
One word. Inconsiderate.


00:07:56.706 --> 00:07:57.844
Or is that two words?


00:07:57.906 --> 00:07:59.445
I can't even look at you right now.


00:07:59.516 --> 00:08:00.616
No, it's one word.


00:08:03.686 --> 00:08:04.946
What just happened?


00:08:05.015 --> 00:08:07.587
Well, for starters, you should
have explained to Bailey.


00:08:07.656 --> 00:08:09.516
That the only reason
you're doing the internship.


00:08:09.586 --> 00:08:10.828
Is because you want to get
a scholarship to Yale?


00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:13.127
That's what was in the letter!


00:08:14.458 --> 00:08:15.557
Why did you drop it then?


00:08:15.627 --> 00:08:17.567
Snacks.
Thanks.


00:08:18.967 --> 00:08:20.697
Hey, Woody. Catch!


00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:21.839
Not very nice.


00:08:21.897 --> 00:08:23.037
Ooh! Sandwich!


00:08:23.109 --> 00:08:24.171
Whoa!


00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.440
Sorry.


00:08:41.061 --> 00:08:44.159
This facility is breathtaking.


00:08:44.228 --> 00:08:46.290
I literally can't breathe.


00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.861
Oh, my. What an
incredible opportunity.


00:08:48.931 --> 00:08:51.301
I'll say. Having one of you
gone over spring break.


00:08:51.369 --> 00:08:53.570
Means half the possibility of disaster.


00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.739
Something I've been longing for
since the dawn of time itself.


00:08:56.811 --> 00:08:58.171
You were in your teens then, right?


00:08:59.441 --> 00:09:00.683
Zack.


00:09:00.742 --> 00:09:03.181
What are you doing here?
And by here, I mean earth!


00:09:04.152 --> 00:09:05.953
London brought me.


00:09:06.022 --> 00:09:07.452
And I thought I'd give you another chance.


00:09:07.522 --> 00:09:08.883
To reconsider the whole car thing.


00:09:08.953 --> 00:09:10.892
Oh, forget it.


00:09:10.954 --> 00:09:13.054
Bailey is still not talking to me.


00:09:13.121 --> 00:09:14.324
Can you blame her?


00:09:14.393 --> 00:09:16.063
No, I can blame you!


00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:21.534
Wouldn't they look cute in a hat?


00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:22.834
Or ks a hat?


00:09:22.903 --> 00:09:24.603
I just love fishies.


00:09:24.676 --> 00:09:27.504
Actually, London, they're not fish.
They're mammals.


00:09:27.572 --> 00:09:29.344
But they don't have humps.


00:09:29.414 --> 00:09:32.715
Not camels. Mammals.
As in they breathe air.


00:09:32.784 --> 00:09:35.646
Fishies do not breathe "air,"
that's why they live in the water.


00:09:35.714 --> 00:09:37.384
They're not fishies.
They're mammals.


00:09:37.455 --> 00:09:38.786
Then why don't they have humps?


00:09:42.295 --> 00:09:44.155
Ooh, yummy!
A fruit plate.


00:09:44.226 --> 00:09:45.425
They must have known I was coming.


00:09:49.766 --> 00:09:53.207
Mmm. Ooh!
This is so delicious.


00:09:53.266 --> 00:09:54.767
Uh, uh... London...


00:10:02.678 --> 00:10:04.747
Ugh!


00:10:04.817 --> 00:10:07.018
I ate fish food!
I ate fish food!


00:10:08.288 --> 00:10:10.188
Actually, it's mammal food.


00:10:10.259 --> 00:10:11.657
Then why don't they have humps?


00:10:15.231 --> 00:10:19.328
Zack, please go away before
you mess this up for me, too.


00:10:19.399 --> 00:10:21.800
Whoa, whoa, whoa, it's
like you don't trust me.


00:10:21.868 --> 00:10:23.739
It's not like that.
It is that.


00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.169
Cody? Cody Martin.


00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:29.439
Welcome. Donald spaulding,
renowned scientist.


00:10:29.509 --> 00:10:31.241
It says so on my parking spot.


00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.651
I know. I saw.
I gushed.


00:10:34.711 --> 00:10:37.681
Sir, I can't tell you how excited
I am about this internship.


00:10:37.752 --> 00:10:40.053
As we are excited to have you.


00:10:40.121 --> 00:10:42.852
Oh, society of super scientists!


00:10:42.923 --> 00:10:44.862
Since I was your age.


00:10:44.922 --> 00:10:47.091
Test tube, beaker, isotope!


00:10:47.163 --> 00:10:49.834
You can't be us and be a dope!


00:10:49.903 --> 00:10:53.034
Go, scientists!
Go, scientists!


00:10:53.103 --> 00:10:54.702
So lame!


00:10:57.843 --> 00:11:00.113
This is my brother, Zack.


00:11:01.944 --> 00:11:03.885
I got the all the brains, and he got...


00:11:04.815 --> 00:11:06.853
Hey, how you doin'?


00:11:06.915 --> 00:11:08.055
Hey, you're ugly.


00:11:10.654 --> 00:11:11.686
Well, nothing, really.


00:11:11.754 --> 00:11:13.255
Mmm.


00:11:13.325 --> 00:11:15.325
Well, follow me, and I'll
show you to the lab.


00:11:16.897 --> 00:11:19.194
Oh, kill me now.


00:11:19.266 --> 00:11:21.336
I designed this entire facility myself,


00:11:21.396 --> 00:11:24.467
So, it's completely state
of the art and wicked cool!


00:11:25.876 --> 00:11:27.835
Well, that looks promising.


00:11:49.529 --> 00:11:52.999
Come on in.
All are welcome. Perfect.


00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:08.621
Hello, there.
I'm Zack Martin.


00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:13.089
You know, I'm having trouble trying to
decide who is cuter, you or the dolphin.


00:12:13.161 --> 00:12:14.360
I'm Nellie.


00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:18.431
Nellie... Nellie, so,
what do you do around here.


00:12:18.491 --> 00:12:21.061
Besides, you know, look amazing?


00:12:21.131 --> 00:12:25.572
I'm a lab tech. Your brother Cody
is doing an internship here, right?


00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.141
Are you as smart as he is?


00:12:27.203 --> 00:12:30.843
Smarter. You know, I recently
posted the highest score ever.


00:12:30.912 --> 00:12:32.242
On kangaroo kaboom.


00:12:33.383 --> 00:12:36.241
So, can you operate that?


00:12:39.025 --> 00:12:42.683
Oh! Let's find out!


00:12:48.264 --> 00:12:50.094
Cody, out of 2,000 applicants,


00:12:50.164 --> 00:12:52.164
Your paper was the most intriguing.


00:12:52.234 --> 00:12:55.205
I almost sent a duplicate in
latin, to show diversity.


00:12:55.265 --> 00:12:58.033
I should have.
I never listen to that voice in my head.


00:12:58.104 --> 00:12:59.835
Mostly because it's in latin.


00:12:59.905 --> 00:13:04.175
Well. A brilliant essay.
"theories of communicating with another species,


00:13:04.245 --> 00:13:06.886
"or what it's like
to have a twin brother."


00:13:06.946 --> 00:13:09.817
The culmination of a lifetime
of unwilling research.


00:13:09.887 --> 00:13:13.354
I know just how you feel.
I have a lesser twin myself.


00:13:13.426 --> 00:13:16.796
I think you'll be inspired by
the research we're working on.


00:13:16.856 --> 00:13:19.358
I'm just inspired that you iron your tie.


00:13:19.426 --> 00:13:21.827
Oh! Me, too!
I iron my pocket hankie.


00:13:21.896 --> 00:13:23.767
No one cares.
Okay.


00:13:23.837 --> 00:13:26.597
Sir, I can't wait to see what
other wonders will unfold.


00:13:26.667 --> 00:13:28.367
Well, I've discovered a rare fruit,


00:13:28.439 --> 00:13:31.477
That, when combined with the
DNA of these jellyfish,


00:13:31.538 --> 00:13:35.008
Could enable dolphins to
telepathically communicate with us,


00:13:35.077 --> 00:13:37.114
Making our two worlds one.


00:13:37.173 --> 00:13:38.214
Do you know what this means?


00:13:38.273 --> 00:13:39.471
That we can talk to dolphins.


00:13:39.542 --> 00:13:40.779
I'm sorry, was that not clear?


00:13:40.839 --> 00:13:42.508
It was clear.
Just very strange.


00:13:42.577 --> 00:13:46.070
No, it isn't.
This could change the world!


00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:49.536
Just imagine it, Cody.
By feeding dolphins this substance,


00:13:49.604 --> 00:13:52.898
We could potentially teach them
about humanity and science,


00:13:52.968 --> 00:13:54.895
And they could teach us about...


00:13:59.668 --> 00:14:00.697
Follow me.


00:14:03.462 --> 00:14:04.757
Zack.


00:14:04.829 --> 00:14:07.453
This is so exciting!
I have so many questions!


00:14:07.525 --> 00:14:09.522
As would Zack, if he were here!


00:14:09.591 --> 00:14:10.590
Not here?


00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:14.026
Zack's not here.


00:14:14.084 --> 00:14:15.352
No, he is not!


00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:18.317
So, why don't I take a casual,
nonchalant little stroll.


00:14:18.387 --> 00:14:20.783
To see if I can locate
the harmless little lad.


00:14:20.853 --> 00:14:22.850
I'll just be right...


00:14:24.615 --> 00:14:26.442
Here they are.


00:14:26.513 --> 00:14:30.816
Obviously, we use dolphins because
they are incredibly intelligent.


00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.962
Except Wally.


00:14:37.032 --> 00:14:40.375
The closer the research
comes to its conclusion,


00:14:40.437 --> 00:14:43.579
The more I know that they
want it as much as we do.


00:14:43.648 --> 00:14:45.350
And exactly how close are you?


00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.382
Just really good friends.
Why? What have you heard?


00:14:48.422 --> 00:14:51.355
I meant, with the research.


00:14:51.425 --> 00:14:53.498
I know. I mean, I knew
that was what you were...


00:14:55.531 --> 00:14:59.571
There are a series of steps to
converging our minds with dolphins.


00:14:59.642 --> 00:15:02.115
But I know you'll be a vital
part of our work here.


00:15:02.174 --> 00:15:05.748
Sir, I'm honored that you've
put such trust in me.


00:15:05.816 --> 00:15:07.361
Just one thing.
Yes?


00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.561
Can I have a name tag?


00:15:10.531 --> 00:15:12.093
How's that?


00:15:12.763 --> 00:15:14.207
Here you go.


00:15:14.265 --> 00:15:15.635
And it's laminated!


00:15:15.707 --> 00:15:17.308
Did it myself.


00:15:17.378 --> 00:15:22.381
These are the most technically
advanced submersibles in the world.


00:15:22.452 --> 00:15:24.855
Why don't you get in and get a feel for it?


00:15:32.071 --> 00:15:34.672
Zack Martin, get out of there this second!


00:15:34.744 --> 00:15:37.417
Don't worry.
I'm not gonna do anything, uh...


00:15:38.817 --> 00:15:40.188
Like that?


00:15:40.247 --> 00:15:41.549
What did you do?


00:15:41.619 --> 00:15:44.022
I don't know.
I just pressed this thing-a-majig.


00:15:44.091 --> 00:15:45.763
And played with this
hoozie-ma-whats,


00:15:45.834 --> 00:15:50.306
And flipped the lever
that said "start."


00:15:50.367 --> 00:15:51.767
That explains it.


00:15:51.839 --> 00:15:55.141
I insist you cease and desist.


00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.384
Okay, fine.
I can unpress th all.


00:15:57.452 --> 00:15:58.955
Don't unpress. Press was bad.


00:15:59.016 --> 00:16:00.627
Unpress, even worse than press.


00:16:00.686 --> 00:16:02.157
Well, I guess we could find out.


00:16:11.976 --> 00:16:16.518
So, it's my understanding
that you graduated from Yale.


00:16:16.589 --> 00:16:17.951
With top honors.


00:16:19.117 --> 00:16:20.792
I know.


00:16:20.862 --> 00:16:24.094
How? I did a little
research of my own.


00:16:24.165 --> 00:16:27.035
Well, now, Yale is begging
me for my research.


00:16:28.938 --> 00:16:29.939
Uh-huh.


00:16:31.007 --> 00:16:33.040
Mmm-hmm. Yes.


00:16:33.108 --> 00:16:36.551
Well, and Harvard, and Princeton,


00:16:36.621 --> 00:16:38.422
And quite a few community colleges.


00:16:43.266 --> 00:16:45.999
And one vocational school.


00:16:46.067 --> 00:16:47.898
As well they should.


00:16:49.169 --> 00:16:50.769
Well, you know, not to brag,


00:16:50.841 --> 00:16:54.081
But do you know what the
other researchers call me?


00:16:54.143 --> 00:16:55.311
Idiot!


00:16:56.115 --> 00:16:59.514
No. Well, not to my face.


00:16:59.588 --> 00:17:01.688
Not you, sir. Him!


00:17:01.755 --> 00:17:02.859
Oh, no!


00:17:07.869 --> 00:17:10.603
Zack! Get out of there!
Can you hear me?


00:17:14.773 --> 00:17:16.546
Oh, Cody!
What are you doing?


00:17:25.891 --> 00:17:28.031
<i>What are you doing?</i>


00:17:28.102 --> 00:17:30.304
<i>Turn around
and go back now!</i>


00:17:30.373 --> 00:17:32.635
<i>Sure, that would be
the not fun option.</i>


00:17:33.946 --> 00:17:35.049
<i>Zack!</i>


00:17:35.108 --> 00:17:37.019
<i>That's
sea Captain Zack to you.</i>


00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:39.419
<i>Whoa!</i>


00:17:40.392 --> 00:17:41.391
<i>Turn around!</i>


00:17:45.663 --> 00:17:47.837
Do something!
Stop them!


00:17:47.894 --> 00:17:49.166
<i>You don't know
what you're doing!</i>


00:17:49.237 --> 00:17:50.665
<i>You don't know
what you're doing!</i>


00:17:50.737 --> 00:17:52.708
Sea wall!
Of course I see the wall.


00:17:52.778 --> 00:17:54.012
It's a big glass wall.


00:17:56.178 --> 00:17:57.480
You're heading towards the sea wall!


00:18:03.195 --> 00:18:05.195
If that sea wall goes,
you'll be sucked out to sea!


00:18:05.256 --> 00:18:06.256
<i>Eject!</i>


00:18:06.325 --> 00:18:07.596
<i>No, you're a reject!</i>


00:18:07.668 --> 00:18:10.028
<i>Not reject,
you, reject! Eject!</i>


00:18:10.699 --> 00:18:11.800
<i>Wall!</i>


00:18:13.112 --> 00:18:15.042
Eject! Eject!


00:18:15.113 --> 00:18:16.843
<i>Eject now! The red button!</i>


00:18:26.199 --> 00:18:28.401
Okay...


00:18:28.461 --> 00:18:30.732
Some of you may look at
this tank as half empty,


00:18:30.803 --> 00:18:32.372
But it's more like a quarter.


00:18:32.434 --> 00:18:34.274
Dr. Spaulding,
I can explain.


00:18:41.588 --> 00:18:42.588
Is that a dolphin?


00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:47.931
Fired! Fired from
my internship.


00:18:47.991 --> 00:18:49.894
There goes my scholarship to Yale.


00:18:49.962 --> 00:18:51.205
And my girlfriend won't even talk to me!


00:18:52.506 --> 00:18:53.976
It's all your fault, Zack!


00:18:54.034 --> 00:18:56.778
Hey, hey, hey, I totally
understand that you feel the need.


00:18:56.849 --> 00:18:59.278
To put the blame on anyone
who happens to be nearby.


00:19:00.221 --> 00:19:02.182
That was my one shot, Zack.


00:19:02.251 --> 00:19:04.922
Look, it looks bad now.


00:19:04.991 --> 00:19:08.426
But we're going to look
back at this and laugh.


00:19:08.495 --> 00:19:12.598
And remember, "he who laughs
last, thinks the slowest."


00:19:12.668 --> 00:19:16.068
This wasn't like all the
other times you messed up.


00:19:16.138 --> 00:19:18.339
This affects my whole my future.


00:19:18.411 --> 00:19:19.513
That's unforgivable.


00:19:19.582 --> 00:19:20.883
Hey, I didn't mean to.


00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:23.854
You never mean to do it,
Zack. You just do it!


00:19:25.226 --> 00:19:27.556
I'll never forgive you
for this! Ever!


00:19:28.796 --> 00:19:29.758
I hate you!


00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.001
That's harsh.


00:19:35.841 --> 00:19:38.374
I'm done, man.
We're through.


00:19:38.444 --> 00:19:41.846
We may be twins, but we are not brothers.


00:19:55.935 --> 00:19:57.474
Did I do a good job, sir?


00:20:06.781 --> 00:20:08.784
Cody and I were supposed to
spend spring break together,


00:20:08.852 --> 00:20:11.284
And he went off to do
something at just he wanted.


00:20:11.352 --> 00:20:12.725
Oh, that is sad.


00:20:13.795 --> 00:20:15.354
You want to count my money?


00:20:15.424 --> 00:20:17.728
You can't have it, but you can count it.


00:20:17.797 --> 00:20:19.366
Oh.


00:20:20.397 --> 00:20:22.741
Ha! It's Cody. Again!


00:20:22.799 --> 00:20:23.903
So, answer him.


00:20:23.973 --> 00:20:25.570
Are you kidding?
And let him off that easy?


00:20:25.642 --> 00:20:26.842
No, think again.


00:20:26.912 --> 00:20:28.544
Okay, I'll try.


00:20:31.515 --> 00:20:32.818
You know, Cody hurt me.


00:20:32.887 --> 00:20:34.417
He abandoned me.


00:20:34.488 --> 00:20:37.527
And now, he needs to know what
it feels like to be ignored.


00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.802
I'm sorry, what?


00:20:39.861 --> 00:20:42.774
Cody won't hear from me
until he's so worried.


00:20:42.834 --> 00:20:45.174
He's trembling like a hound
dog pushing out a peach pit.


00:20:45.245 --> 00:20:48.675
Ha! I am woman,
hear me ignore!


00:20:48.745 --> 00:20:49.748
I'm sorry, what?


00:20:57.362 --> 00:20:59.665
Oh, thanks!
They're Arturo vitali.


00:20:59.735 --> 00:21:01.093
They're made from eel skin.


00:21:02.236 --> 00:21:04.267
I hope they're not anybody you know.


00:21:14.654 --> 00:21:16.625
Cody, there you are.


00:21:16.695 --> 00:21:18.323
Go away!


00:21:18.393 --> 00:21:21.738
Didn't you get my e-mail about me
constructing my emotional borders.


00:21:21.798 --> 00:21:24.769
Forbidding you from entering
the country that is my soul?


00:21:24.837 --> 00:21:26.970
All your e-mails go
directly to trash.


00:21:27.042 --> 00:21:29.812
Besides, I think you're gonna cheer
up once you see who I've found.


00:21:32.453 --> 00:21:33.814
Good day,
Mr. Martin.


00:21:33.884 --> 00:21:35.054
Dr. Spaulding?
Yes.


00:21:35.125 --> 00:21:37.256
What are you doing here?


00:21:37.326 --> 00:21:40.758
Well, although there is no chance
you'll ever work for me again, ever,


00:21:40.829 --> 00:21:43.902
In this, or in any parallel universe,


00:21:43.972 --> 00:21:45.442
There is another internship.


00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.805
That I think you're right for.


00:21:47.873 --> 00:21:51.516
Are you serious? Don't toy with me now.
I'm fragile and broken.


00:21:51.584 --> 00:21:53.287
No, I'm quite serious.


00:21:53.346 --> 00:21:55.988
It would be a shame to see
your talents go to waste.


00:21:56.059 --> 00:21:57.990
Sir, you don't know
how much this means to me,


00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.458
Just getting a second chance.


00:21:59.531 --> 00:22:02.632
Well, the gemini project,
about 50 miles from us,


00:22:02.702 --> 00:22:04.263
Is an isolated science camp.


00:22:04.332 --> 00:22:08.075
Doing research similar
to ours, but on twins.


00:22:08.145 --> 00:22:10.577
I'm a twin!
The superior twin. Yes.


00:22:10.648 --> 00:22:12.449
It's true.
I'm proof.


00:22:13.548 --> 00:22:14.680
You certainly are.


00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.620
Well, I sent your application paper.


00:22:17.689 --> 00:22:20.465
To the scientist
who runs it, Dr. Olsen.


00:22:20.535 --> 00:22:22.366
He was quite excited.


00:22:22.435 --> 00:22:23.566
There's just one thing.


00:22:23.637 --> 00:22:25.037
Anything.
I'll do anything.


00:22:25.107 --> 00:22:29.679
Well, because the work Dr.
Olsen is doing is on twins,


00:22:29.738 --> 00:22:31.850
You and your brother would need to attend.


00:22:31.912 --> 00:22:34.012
Just not that thing.


00:22:35.984 --> 00:22:38.757
That is Dr. Olsen's
one requirement.


00:22:38.824 --> 00:22:42.628
After reading your paper, he thinks
that you could be the ideal twins.


00:22:42.698 --> 00:22:44.196
To participate in his research.


00:22:44.267 --> 00:22:47.640
Me and Zack? In a lab?


00:22:47.711 --> 00:22:49.742
Hey, it's not like I'm just some idiot.


00:22:49.808 --> 00:22:51.374
Who doesn't know anything about science.


00:22:51.444 --> 00:22:53.345
Oh, yeah? What's matter?


00:22:53.414 --> 00:22:55.155
Nothing.
What's the matter with you?


00:22:55.214 --> 00:22:56.716
See? See?


00:22:56.786 --> 00:22:58.588
I can't go anywhere with him.


00:22:58.656 --> 00:23:00.759
Yeah? Well, I don't wanna
go anywhere with you first!


00:23:00.828 --> 00:23:02.359
And when I get there, you're not welcome!


00:23:02.928 --> 00:23:04.228
Ouch.


00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:06.002
Well, that is a shame.


00:23:11.245 --> 00:23:14.847
You know, this internship
could help you qualify.


00:23:14.916 --> 00:23:16.549
For a scholarship to Yale.


00:23:16.618 --> 00:23:18.019
It would?


00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:22.692
Cody, are you really going to let
your anger towards your brother.


00:23:22.762 --> 00:23:24.533
Jeopardize your entire future?


00:23:51.638 --> 00:23:52.839
Is this your lunch?


00:23:53.341 --> 00:23:55.013
Oh, it was.


00:23:55.080 --> 00:23:56.510
Cody, next time you throw up,


00:23:56.582 --> 00:23:58.725
At least tell me so I can grab my camera.


00:23:58.784 --> 00:24:01.624
Oh, I love you, dock.


00:24:02.396 --> 00:24:04.728
Oh. Mmm.


00:24:04.798 --> 00:24:07.000
You must be the Martin
twins, Zack and Cody.


00:24:07.071 --> 00:24:11.199
Oh, hi. I'm Cody.


00:24:11.271 --> 00:24:12.842
It's an honor
to meet you, Dr. Olsen.


00:24:12.914 --> 00:24:15.615
I know. Come on, I have
so much to show you.


00:24:15.684 --> 00:24:16.985
Come on, don't dawdle.


00:24:20.387 --> 00:24:21.388
Come on.


00:24:25.629 --> 00:24:26.661
Let me help you with that.


00:24:26.729 --> 00:24:28.433
Oh, it's really heavy.
Watch out.


00:24:31.147 --> 00:24:33.406
Yeah. This way.


00:24:33.475 --> 00:24:37.015
I think you're both gonna see that
this is someplace very special.


00:24:38.688 --> 00:24:40.289
I'll say.


00:24:40.347 --> 00:24:42.219
This facility is fantastic.


00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:44.463
This was actually
an abandoned mill complex.


00:24:44.530 --> 00:24:46.963
The actual sawmill is on the
other side of the Lake.


00:24:47.034 --> 00:24:48.503
We're planning on renovating it.


00:24:48.565 --> 00:24:50.566
I have two words for you
that might change your life.


00:24:50.636 --> 00:24:51.978
Hot. Tub.


00:24:52.037 --> 00:24:54.677
There you go.
My contribution to science.


00:24:54.748 --> 00:24:58.420
Now, I must warn you.
My brother's idea of research.


00:24:58.481 --> 00:25:01.253
Is discovering how to
simultaneously burp and sneeze.


00:25:01.321 --> 00:25:03.555
I can almost do it without
my eyes popping out.


00:25:03.624 --> 00:25:05.366
You must be very proud.


00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:14.922
Welcome to the most advanced.


00:25:14.992 --> 00:25:19.224
Subterranean neuroscientific
laboratory on earth.


00:25:19.293 --> 00:25:23.064
Gentlemen, I give you the gemini project.


00:25:23.135 --> 00:25:25.163
It kind of just looks
like a giant basement.


00:25:25.235 --> 00:25:26.505
So, you don't think it's too much?


00:25:26.567 --> 00:25:28.837
Well, it doesn't
really scream "science."


00:25:28.908 --> 00:25:30.105
'cause I decorated it myself.


00:25:30.176 --> 00:25:33.178
Is that the hydro-isotope
caloubometer,


00:25:33.248 --> 00:25:37.448
Capable of reading the
undetectable electrical charges.


00:25:37.518 --> 00:25:38.950
In a miniscule brain wave?


00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:40.521
Yes. Isn't she beautiful?


00:25:40.590 --> 00:25:42.492
Oh, I love her.


00:25:43.664 --> 00:25:45.131
Oh. Shh.


00:25:46.532 --> 00:25:47.732
Baby, don't speak.


00:25:47.802 --> 00:25:50.464
Cody, come, come, this way.
I have to show you this.


00:25:51.875 --> 00:25:56.248
This is my mind transference facilitator.


00:25:56.308 --> 00:25:59.678
Every apparatus in this
shangri-la of science...


00:25:59.746 --> 00:26:00.978
It's astounding.


00:26:01.048 --> 00:26:02.118
What's this?


00:26:02.188 --> 00:26:03.818
Uh, that's a cappuccino machine.


00:26:03.889 --> 00:26:05.160
Dibs on this.


00:26:07.188 --> 00:26:09.160
And dibs on these.


00:26:09.232 --> 00:26:10.631
Hey, hey, Nellie.


00:26:10.693 --> 00:26:13.663
Nellie. I'm Zack.
Remember me?


00:26:13.732 --> 00:26:15.873
I crashed that trillion dollar sub.


00:26:15.934 --> 00:26:18.003
Kind of a legend in the science world.


00:26:18.076 --> 00:26:20.575
Hello, Zack.
This is my sister, kellie.


00:26:20.646 --> 00:26:23.814
We sometimes help Dr.
Spaulding with his work as well.


00:26:23.875 --> 00:26:26.116
Since the research is so similar.


00:26:28.988 --> 00:26:31.587
So, what exactly are you working on?


00:26:31.658 --> 00:26:34.730
My colleague,
Dr. Spaulding,


00:26:34.801 --> 00:26:36.962
Is developing a substance
that will allow dolphins.


00:26:37.032 --> 00:26:40.101
To communicate with humans telepathically.


00:26:40.172 --> 00:26:42.172
It's Noble, sure, it's Noble,


00:26:42.242 --> 00:26:46.544
But my goal is to use it to perfect
communication between humans.


00:26:46.613 --> 00:26:48.417
For what result?


00:26:48.484 --> 00:26:50.786
Imagine. If we could connect
with each other's minds,


00:26:50.846 --> 00:26:53.716
We'd actually be able to
feel what others feel.


00:26:53.786 --> 00:26:57.988
And where there's more empathy between
people, there's less conflict.


00:26:58.057 --> 00:27:00.430
So you chose Zack and me.


00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:02.430
Because we have conflict?


00:27:02.499 --> 00:27:05.001
Exactly! Now, initially
my research was on twins.


00:27:05.070 --> 00:27:06.439
Because of your similar DNA,


00:27:06.499 --> 00:27:08.613
But it's progressed far beyond that.


00:27:08.673 --> 00:27:12.384
If I can resolve the irresolvable conflicts.


00:27:12.442 --> 00:27:14.544
Between twins such as yourselves,


00:27:14.614 --> 00:27:17.687
I can expand that to all mankind,


00:27:17.757 --> 00:27:22.298
And create a world free of fighting,
and anger, and aggression.


00:27:22.357 --> 00:27:24.456
Well, that'll make hockey fun.


00:27:24.529 --> 00:27:27.127
Perhaps it will be better if I show you.


00:27:27.198 --> 00:27:29.669
So, why am I wired up to this thing again?


00:27:29.739 --> 00:27:33.341
I need to establish a baseline
for your brain processing speed.


00:27:33.410 --> 00:27:37.183
Why even bother?
He's asked that question three times.


00:27:37.241 --> 00:27:42.482
Now, Zack, words will flash on the
screen in a series of colors.


00:27:42.553 --> 00:27:48.526
Red, green, blue... But the color of the
letters won't correspond to the word.


00:27:48.596 --> 00:27:50.998
For example, the word
"blue" is written in red.


00:27:51.066 --> 00:27:52.598
Can this thing kill asteroids?


00:27:52.668 --> 00:27:53.838
No.


00:27:53.899 --> 00:27:55.098
Kind of a waste of money then.


00:27:55.169 --> 00:27:57.069
You see what I have to live with?


00:27:57.141 --> 00:28:00.444
Zack, your job is to
correctly touch the color.


00:28:00.508 --> 00:28:02.652
The word is spelling in the allotted time.


00:28:04.214 --> 00:28:05.522
Got it!
Really?


00:28:05.580 --> 00:28:06.984
No. No.
No?


00:28:10.355 --> 00:28:11.425
Did you get all the brains?


00:28:11.495 --> 00:28:12.494
Yeah. Pretty much.


00:28:13.865 --> 00:28:15.639
Ow!


00:28:15.695 --> 00:28:17.696
Keep in mind that if you
don't respond fast enough,


00:28:17.767 --> 00:28:19.738
The machine administers a small shock.


00:28:19.808 --> 00:28:21.568
Okay. Wait, what?


00:28:22.675 --> 00:28:24.979
Cody, you register reply times.


00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:26.281
Mmm-hmm.


00:28:26.349 --> 00:28:27.578
This is going to be fun.


00:28:29.282 --> 00:28:31.152
So, uh...


00:28:31.692 --> 00:28:32.692
Okay.


00:28:34.252 --> 00:28:35.250
Huh.


00:28:37.424 --> 00:28:40.334
What do I win?
Mom and dad's car?


00:28:45.275 --> 00:28:47.309
Ow! Ooh, that hurt.


00:28:47.377 --> 00:28:49.810
Concentrate.
Next one's up.


00:28:51.178 --> 00:28:52.578
Hey, that's not fair, I was talking.


00:28:52.647 --> 00:28:55.080
Yeah, that's usually
where your troubles begin.


00:29:00.662 --> 00:29:02.234
Ow. I felt that one
in my toes.


00:29:03.693 --> 00:29:05.131
Ow! Ow!


00:29:07.207 --> 00:29:08.404
Ow!


00:29:08.475 --> 00:29:10.506
Get them right
and there won't be a problem.


00:29:14.005 --> 00:29:17.278
How can I... How can I get them
right if they're moving too fast?


00:29:19.949 --> 00:29:22.259
Oh, very disappointing results...


00:29:24.531 --> 00:29:26.361
Hey, take your revenge now.


00:29:26.432 --> 00:29:28.130
As long as this makes us...
Ow! ...Even.


00:29:31.503 --> 00:29:34.974
Let's get one thing straight.
We will never be even.


00:29:46.258 --> 00:29:47.042
You know, right about now,


00:29:47.697 --> 00:29:50.449
Cody and I would be romantically
feasting on edible fungi.


00:29:50.504 --> 00:29:53.435
We picked off the organically
fertilized forest floor.


00:29:53.509 --> 00:29:55.522
Wow.
You're a cheap date.


00:29:55.595 --> 00:29:57.258
But none of that matters now.


00:29:57.320 --> 00:29:59.509
Yeah, because Cody made his choice,


00:29:59.584 --> 00:30:01.839
And he chose science over chemistry.


00:30:01.913 --> 00:30:04.312
Did it ever occur to you that he
might have had a very good reason...


00:30:04.387 --> 00:30:05.840
You know what?
Not good enough.


00:30:05.905 --> 00:30:06.048
But if you two could just communicate...


00:30:06.073 --> 00:30:06.205
You know what, after this moment,


00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:09.044
I'm done talking about Cody.


00:30:09.094 --> 00:30:10.159
Works for me.


00:30:10.227 --> 00:30:11.814
I am in.
Great.


00:30:12.835 --> 00:30:15.555
Aw, look at the cute crabs.


00:30:15.623 --> 00:30:18.531
Oh, that one looks just
like my Uncle carmine.


00:30:18.599 --> 00:30:20.682
He had those same beady red eyes,


00:30:20.754 --> 00:30:23.500
And claw-like hands,
and scaly complexion.


00:30:23.559 --> 00:30:24.920
Oh.


00:30:24.988 --> 00:30:26.108
It's okay, it's okay.


00:30:26.176 --> 00:30:27.536
He met a woman who looks
just like a lobster.


00:30:27.596 --> 00:30:28.994
Now, they're really happy together.


00:30:29.053 --> 00:30:31.651
No. Cody loves crabs.


00:30:31.723 --> 00:30:34.519
Especially, that little bib you
get to wear when you eat them.


00:30:34.590 --> 00:30:36.825
He calls it his
"crustacean catcher."


00:30:36.887 --> 00:30:38.825
You two are a barnyard full of crazy.


00:30:41.294 --> 00:30:42.561
Okay, good luck!


00:30:43.490 --> 00:30:44.559
Good luck with what?


00:30:47.089 --> 00:30:49.592
Fine. Keep your claws on.
I won't tell them.


00:30:49.653 --> 00:30:50.692
Tell us what?


00:30:50.752 --> 00:30:51.851
About the escape.


00:30:51.920 --> 00:30:53.192
Escape? What escape?


00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:56.059
If I told you I wouldn't
"not be telling you!" hello!


00:30:58.824 --> 00:31:00.622
Sorry, boys.
You're about to be lunch.


00:31:04.058 --> 00:31:05.928
We got a runner!
We got a runner!


00:31:05.989 --> 00:31:07.483
Sit!


00:31:07.555 --> 00:31:10.322
Boo, you, little crabby!
Boo, you!


00:31:10.391 --> 00:31:11.388
Help.


00:31:23.419 --> 00:31:24.520
Salt?


00:31:24.588 --> 00:31:25.825
Thank you.


00:31:27.827 --> 00:31:30.024
More water?
Read my mind!


00:31:35.057 --> 00:31:36.128
Napkin?


00:31:36.187 --> 00:31:37.257
Oh, absolutely!


00:31:39.052 --> 00:31:42.421
You guys are all so nice to each other.


00:31:42.492 --> 00:31:45.188
Why wouldn't we be?
That's what I was going to say!


00:31:46.882 --> 00:31:49.057
Twins should always be nice to each other,


00:31:49.123 --> 00:31:50.451
Don't you agree, Ben and sven?


00:31:50.520 --> 00:31:51.885
Yeah.
Yeah.


00:31:51.954 --> 00:31:56.008
We love being twins.
Don't you?


00:31:56.067 --> 00:32:00.415
Well, if by love you mean
a dark bottomless pit.


00:32:00.486 --> 00:32:05.905
Of constant burning of a thousand
white hot suns, then yes.


00:32:05.974 --> 00:32:07.995
So, you two don't get along?


00:32:08.067 --> 00:32:11.182
Sure. We got a long...
List of things that.


00:32:11.250 --> 00:32:13.081
We can't stand about each other.


00:32:13.141 --> 00:32:15.604
Well, you know, how can I
get along with someone.


00:32:15.671 --> 00:32:17.862
Who's constantly ruining my life?


00:32:17.931 --> 00:32:21.286
Or someone who is constantly
telling you what's wrong?


00:32:21.356 --> 00:32:23.108
Well, everything you do is wrong!


00:32:23.177 --> 00:32:24.967
Oh, like coming here to help you?


00:32:25.037 --> 00:32:26.731
Oh, please.
You only did that.


00:32:26.802 --> 00:32:28.664
Because I agreed to give you
mom and dad's car if you did!


00:32:28.721 --> 00:32:30.118
Only because you had no other choice!


00:32:30.188 --> 00:32:32.718
Zack, Cody, you're twins.


00:32:32.776 --> 00:32:34.338
Why are you hurting each other?


00:32:34.407 --> 00:32:37.366
Yeah, hurting each other...


00:32:37.424 --> 00:32:38.689
Hurts each other.


00:32:38.760 --> 00:32:39.984
Yeah.
Yeah.


00:32:40.053 --> 00:32:41.745
It would be the same as hurting...


00:32:43.109 --> 00:32:44.373
Yourself.


00:32:45.499 --> 00:32:47.856
No, no, I don't really agree.


00:32:47.927 --> 00:32:51.015
Let me demonstrate.
See, if I pinch Zack...


00:32:53.306 --> 00:32:55.506
It doesn't cause me any pain.


00:32:55.563 --> 00:32:59.559
And if I, for example, splash this glass
of ice-cold water in Cody's face,


00:33:01.778 --> 00:33:04.636
I don't feel anything.
Thirsty, dry even.


00:33:06.396 --> 00:33:10.081
And if I flip Zack out of his chair.


00:33:10.153 --> 00:33:11.985
Using the element of surprise...


00:33:17.897 --> 00:33:19.887
See? I feel nothing.


00:33:21.350 --> 00:33:22.903
I've proved my point!


00:33:39.951 --> 00:33:42.835
So, uh, whose grandmother
is missing a finger?


00:33:44.937 --> 00:33:49.086
These look worse than
mom's apricot tuna roll ups.


00:33:49.149 --> 00:33:52.043
This is the corsican fruit,
the key to all my research.


00:33:54.302 --> 00:33:56.357
I guarantee you'll find it's the most
delicious fruit you've ever tasted.


00:33:56.426 --> 00:33:57.949
More delicious than mango?
Yes.


00:33:58.019 --> 00:33:59.384
More delicious than blueberries?
Yes.


00:33:59.454 --> 00:34:00.805
More delicious than...
Just eat it.


00:34:10.114 --> 00:34:11.937
That is amazing!


00:34:12.830 --> 00:34:14.899
Yeah, it's like...


00:34:14.964 --> 00:34:16.625
It's like it slithered down my throat,


00:34:16.683 --> 00:34:19.443
And sent my tummy into a yummy frenzy.


00:34:19.515 --> 00:34:22.341
It is like, right before
it entered my mouth,


00:34:22.402 --> 00:34:25.528
It swirled around the
world's largest lollipop.


00:34:25.599 --> 00:34:27.947
It's like my tongue just
took a bath in a rainbow.


00:34:28.017 --> 00:34:30.543
Mine just swam in a peach nectar River.


00:34:30.613 --> 00:34:32.738
A peach nectar River?
Seriously?


00:34:32.805 --> 00:34:34.764
Oh, like you can take a bath in a rainbow!


00:34:44.634 --> 00:34:46.286
Mmm, Bailey...


00:34:48.486 --> 00:34:50.407
Please forgive me.


00:34:50.476 --> 00:34:52.369
Cody wuv Bailey.


00:34:53.196 --> 00:34:55.057
Does Bailey wuv Cody?


00:34:55.127 --> 00:34:57.746
Ow! Oh, no, my fingers don't
bend that way, Bailey, stop!


00:35:03.667 --> 00:35:06.059
Why'd you hit me?


00:35:06.116 --> 00:35:10.040
I didn't hit you.
I must've just fell.


00:35:10.111 --> 00:35:12.498
Then why does my arm hurt?


00:35:12.568 --> 00:35:16.023
I guess I hit it on the way down.


00:35:16.083 --> 00:35:18.280
Let's just go to sleep.


00:35:18.343 --> 00:35:22.363
You go to sleep.
No, you go to sleep.


00:35:22.435 --> 00:35:24.752
Oh, I really need to call Bailey.


00:35:24.825 --> 00:35:26.146
I thought she was annoyed with you?


00:35:26.217 --> 00:35:28.706
Her and I finally had something in common.


00:35:28.777 --> 00:35:32.601
Well, she was. That's why I decided
to give her all that time.


00:35:32.659 --> 00:35:34.123
You know, it's scientifically proven,


00:35:34.194 --> 00:35:36.019
You never confront a
woman when she's angry.


00:35:36.083 --> 00:35:37.310
Or calm, for that matter.


00:35:38.215 --> 00:35:40.138
Oh, Cody...


00:35:41.500 --> 00:35:43.621
No cell phones.


00:35:43.694 --> 00:35:46.053
It's one of the few rules
we have around here.


00:35:46.122 --> 00:35:47.414
I really need to call my girlfriend.


00:35:47.485 --> 00:35:48.679
It's impossible.


00:35:48.738 --> 00:35:51.069
I know, right?
No, no, no, it's true.


00:35:51.141 --> 00:35:53.758
He has a girlfriend.
Well, he had a girlfriend.


00:35:56.513 --> 00:35:58.974
No, what I meant was that the
cell phone's microwave radiation.


00:35:59.043 --> 00:36:01.266
May affect some of our
more delicate instruments.


00:36:01.331 --> 00:36:03.096
We wouldn't wanna risk a malfunction.


00:36:08.014 --> 00:36:09.707
Good man.


00:36:09.767 --> 00:36:11.697
I hope you both slept well.
Today, I'm going to be observing.


00:36:11.765 --> 00:36:14.018
While you both perform a series of
sports and training exercises...


00:36:14.088 --> 00:36:15.620
Pass.


00:36:15.681 --> 00:36:17.312
Actually, he can't pass.


00:36:17.381 --> 00:36:20.097
Or run, or kick, or hit, or score...


00:36:20.170 --> 00:36:22.967
Sports and I have
a complicated relationship.


00:36:23.109 --> 00:36:25.458
Walking and you have
a complicated relationship.


00:36:25.645 --> 00:36:28.374
Still, it may provide valuable insights.


00:36:28.432 --> 00:36:31.353
As to how well twins
work together as a unit.


00:36:34.850 --> 00:36:37.298
Well, I guess if it's
for science, then okay.


00:36:37.365 --> 00:36:38.373
Good man.


00:37:02.085 --> 00:37:03.506
Hey, here's a fun fact.


00:37:03.584 --> 00:37:05.945
You can actually hit the
ball with these things.


00:37:06.007 --> 00:37:08.657
Oh, hit it?
I couldn't even see the thing.


00:37:15.362 --> 00:37:17.507
How come we don't have matching outfits?


00:37:18.515 --> 00:37:19.745
You sicken me.


00:37:30.541 --> 00:37:32.240
Watch it!
Hey, you watch it.


00:37:37.709 --> 00:37:38.710
No.


00:37:57.530 --> 00:37:59.212
It's okay. You'll do...


00:37:59.275 --> 00:38:00.557
Better next time.


00:38:00.627 --> 00:38:01.806
Yeah.
Yeah.


00:38:01.865 --> 00:38:03.382
The double team!
The double team!


00:38:04.935 --> 00:38:06.251
They seem weird to you?


00:38:06.320 --> 00:38:07.330
I think they're nice.


00:38:27.505 --> 00:38:29.048
Yeah!
Yeah!


00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:30.129
Here goes nothing.


00:38:32.282 --> 00:38:33.490
Whoa!


00:38:33.557 --> 00:38:34.804
Ow!


00:38:39.455 --> 00:38:41.508
No, I'm climbing back down.


00:38:41.576 --> 00:38:43.367
Are you serious?


00:38:43.436 --> 00:38:46.261
Well, actually, I'm a little
more introspective.


00:38:46.329 --> 00:38:48.145
If they can do it, we can.


00:38:50.168 --> 00:38:51.680
Don't look down!


00:38:54.919 --> 00:38:58.181
Man, you're so weak.
How do you even button your shirt?


00:38:58.250 --> 00:39:00.339
My muscles are crying.


00:39:00.401 --> 00:39:02.632
It's called sweat!


00:39:02.693 --> 00:39:04.953
Don't fall, Cody.
Cody, don't fall! Cody!


00:39:05.021 --> 00:39:06.396
I'm falling!


00:39:09.334 --> 00:39:11.250
I'm falling, I'm falling!


00:39:15.863 --> 00:39:18.417
Are you feeling something weird?


00:39:18.490 --> 00:39:20.171
Can't a guy scratch in peace?


00:39:21.013 --> 00:39:22.938
No, not that.


00:39:22.998 --> 00:39:26.001
I'm feeling whatever you're feeling.


00:39:26.070 --> 00:39:28.791
You know how crazy this is?


00:39:28.862 --> 00:39:32.025
Forget it. I've flossed with
thicker strings than this.


00:39:32.094 --> 00:39:33.849
What do they have that we don't have?


00:39:33.905 --> 00:39:36.910
Lack of fear, upper body strength.


00:39:36.980 --> 00:39:38.727
Wills that are notarized.


00:39:38.797 --> 00:39:41.223
Trust me,
I'm a five-star athlete.


00:39:50.960 --> 00:39:52.979
My leg is
falling asleep. Oh, no!


00:39:53.048 --> 00:39:55.230
My leg is falling
asleep, too. Push!


00:39:56.380 --> 00:39:58.396
I am pushing.
You push!


00:39:58.469 --> 00:39:59.710
You know I have weak wrists!


00:40:09.008 --> 00:40:10.385
No, no, no.
Don't take it!


00:40:10.460 --> 00:40:12.639
Every fallen petal is gonna represent.


00:40:12.711 --> 00:40:14.832
One more phone call you don't get from him.


00:40:17.325 --> 00:40:20.694
Maybe Cody hasn't called because
his phone ran out of battery,


00:40:20.767 --> 00:40:23.664
Or he's been abducted by aliens,


00:40:23.725 --> 00:40:25.435
Or a secret society of pilgrims,


00:40:25.511 --> 00:40:28.509
Disguised as aliens so we don't
know that they're pilgrims.


00:40:28.579 --> 00:40:30.798
And you really think that's possible?


00:40:30.869 --> 00:40:33.564
Sure! People's phones run out
of battery all the time!


00:40:33.625 --> 00:40:35.884
No, no, no. See, Cody
stopped calling me.


00:40:35.957 --> 00:40:37.975
Just becau I was ignoring him.


00:40:38.038 --> 00:40:40.094
Well, lots of people ignore me.


00:40:40.162 --> 00:40:43.022
Just do what I do.
Ignore them back.


00:40:43.094 --> 00:40:46.323
Except I'm not sure if they notice
because they're ignoring me.


00:40:46.392 --> 00:40:49.087
He thinks by not calling me after
I didn't answer his calls,


00:40:49.158 --> 00:40:51.914
That I'll be weakened, call him,


00:40:51.984 --> 00:40:53.671
And then he doesn't have to call me again.


00:40:53.734 --> 00:40:55.415
But didn't he call you the first time?


00:40:55.485 --> 00:40:57.301
Only so I could ignore him.


00:40:57.376 --> 00:40:58.917
He thinks he's the ultimate strategist.


00:41:00.334 --> 00:41:01.947
But like my grammy Pickett says,


00:41:02.019 --> 00:41:05.316
"you can put your boots in the oven,
but that don't make 'em biscuits."


00:41:05.389 --> 00:41:07.074
Unless you add flour and eggs.


00:41:07.137 --> 00:41:08.386
I mean, sure, they're still chewy, but...


00:41:08.449 --> 00:41:11.009
You know what? Game on, Cody.
I'll show him.


00:41:11.086 --> 00:41:12.826
What are you going to do?


00:41:16.024 --> 00:41:17.581
Check this.


00:41:18.992 --> 00:41:20.478
Not the big "d."


00:41:20.579 --> 00:41:23.434
Oh, yes. Oh,
it must be done.


00:41:23.504 --> 00:41:24.951
I can't watch.
Tell me when it's over.


00:41:26.275 --> 00:41:29.129
Cody Martin, you are now and forever...


00:41:31.896 --> 00:41:33.305
...Deleted!


00:41:38.776 --> 00:41:41.291
Dr. Olsen,


00:41:41.352 --> 00:41:47.562
Zack and I have been experiencing
some strange phenomenon.


00:41:47.633 --> 00:41:49.364
Seems almost a little too improbable.


00:41:49.434 --> 00:41:50.463
I feel what he feels.


00:41:50.536 --> 00:41:52.439
Why must you complicate everything?


00:41:52.505 --> 00:41:55.680
Well, it wouldn't be complicated if
you didn't only have one brain cell.


00:41:55.739 --> 00:41:57.180
Which is going to die alone.


00:41:57.251 --> 00:41:59.181
This is perfect.
This is better than perfect.


00:41:59.252 --> 00:42:01.422
Wait a minute.
What's better than perfect?


00:42:01.482 --> 00:42:03.223
Let's stick with perfect.
Come with me.


00:42:05.092 --> 00:42:08.527
Just to be clear, I'm hooked up
to this thing again because?


00:42:08.596 --> 00:42:10.068
The results should be different this time.


00:42:10.137 --> 00:42:11.370
Starting.


00:42:18.242 --> 00:42:19.444
Ow!


00:42:19.513 --> 00:42:20.955
What are you complaining about?


00:42:21.013 --> 00:42:22.515
I'm the one who got shocked.


00:42:22.587 --> 00:42:24.160
I definitely felt pain.


00:42:27.159 --> 00:42:28.531
Ow!
Ow!


00:42:29.728 --> 00:42:31.773
Would you stop that?
No, you stop it!


00:42:31.834 --> 00:42:33.802
It's the effects of the corsican fruit.


00:42:33.872 --> 00:42:37.377
When eaten by twins, it creates
a telepathic communication.


00:42:37.444 --> 00:42:38.517
That's genius.


00:42:38.577 --> 00:42:41.147
Yes, it is.
And that's only stage one.


00:42:41.218 --> 00:42:44.520
Zack, Cody, are you ready for stage two?


00:42:44.588 --> 00:42:45.759
Yes, we are.


00:42:45.820 --> 00:42:47.831
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hold the Joy buzzer.


00:42:47.889 --> 00:42:49.534
What's stage two?


00:42:49.591 --> 00:42:51.904
Empathy.
Creating an emotional connection.


00:42:51.965 --> 00:42:54.307
Where stage one created a physical one.


00:42:55.805 --> 00:42:57.077
Are you prepared?


00:42:57.146 --> 00:42:58.978
Yes. Ow!


00:42:59.048 --> 00:43:02.382
That's a no.
No. That's a yes. Ow!


00:43:02.449 --> 00:43:04.488
I heard a no.
Dr. Olsen has vision!


00:43:08.894 --> 00:43:12.069
Just like you to run off
before you finish something.


00:43:12.167 --> 00:43:14.670
Oh yeah? Well, I'm finished
being a human lightning rod.


00:43:14.739 --> 00:43:16.707
By now, I can recharge my own cell phone.


00:43:16.780 --> 00:43:19.485
You know, if you leave,
I can't finish my internship.


00:43:19.545 --> 00:43:21.251
But you couldn't care less, could you?


00:43:21.310 --> 00:43:23.983
Wow, Cody. Actually,
I could care less.


00:43:24.055 --> 00:43:26.988
And I'm sick of you blaming me for
everything that goes wrong in your life.


00:43:27.057 --> 00:43:29.259
I only do that because you are to blame!


00:43:29.325 --> 00:43:30.797
Yeah?


00:43:30.871 --> 00:43:33.573
Give me one example
of how I ruined your life!


00:43:33.643 --> 00:43:34.898
Two weeks...
That doesn't count.


00:43:34.970 --> 00:43:36.271
What about when...
Nope, not that time either.


00:43:36.343 --> 00:43:38.743
Fine. If you hadn't
completely messed up.


00:43:38.813 --> 00:43:40.575
My internship
with Dr. Spaulding,


00:43:40.645 --> 00:43:43.288
I could be there, as far
away from you as possible.


00:43:43.350 --> 00:43:45.061
That's not my fault,


00:43:45.117 --> 00:43:46.958
Because if you had just given
me the car in the first place


00:43:47.028 --> 00:43:49.658
I wouldn't have needed to
follow you down to spaulding's.


00:43:49.731 --> 00:43:51.130
To make you change your mind!


00:43:51.201 --> 00:43:53.231
A car you're never gonna see now!


00:43:53.302 --> 00:43:55.905
Oh, ok. Cool. Cool guy.
Goodbye, Cody.


00:43:57.005 --> 00:43:58.647
Fine, go!


00:43:58.705 --> 00:44:01.850
Just one more on the list of
things I'll never forgive you for.


00:44:01.918 --> 00:44:04.080
You know, out of all the twins I
could have gotten stuck with,


00:44:04.148 --> 00:44:05.319
Why did it have to be you?


00:44:07.891 --> 00:44:11.393
Oh. Because you think
it's so easy.


00:44:11.465 --> 00:44:13.865
To be the twin of a guy who actually cares.


00:44:13.936 --> 00:44:16.466
Why a carrot is more orange than an orange!


00:44:21.550 --> 00:44:23.112
Yeah?
How about this?


00:44:23.180 --> 00:44:24.681
Don't you do it!


00:44:24.753 --> 00:44:26.626
Take that digit away
from that nasal vestibule.


00:44:28.726 --> 00:44:30.899
Unsanitary! Unsanitary.


00:44:33.837 --> 00:44:36.200
You know that sound
that you just love so much?


00:44:36.268 --> 00:44:38.041
No, don't do it!
Don't do it, Cody.


00:44:38.110 --> 00:44:39.642
Here it comes.


00:44:39.712 --> 00:44:41.443
Ooh, cracking!


00:44:46.887 --> 00:44:49.987
Oh, yeah?
How about this, huh?


00:44:51.629 --> 00:44:54.132
That's not fair. Zack, that's not fair.
I'm wearing briefs!


00:44:54.204 --> 00:44:58.074
Yeah, well, now they'll have a nice
runway for when you take them off!


00:45:03.946 --> 00:45:06.617
Yeah? You ready for this?
You're not even gonna see this coming.


00:45:32.725 --> 00:45:33.866
Are you leaving?


00:45:33.936 --> 00:45:36.440
I wouldn't say leaving.
More escaping.


00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:37.669
Can we go for a walk first?


00:45:37.739 --> 00:45:39.541
I can't.
I really have to...


00:45:44.153 --> 00:45:45.655
After you.


00:45:50.428 --> 00:45:52.701
It's hard to be a twin, huh?


00:45:52.759 --> 00:45:55.731
No. It's hard
to be Cody's twin.


00:45:55.801 --> 00:45:57.972
Being kellie's twin
looks like a lot of fun.


00:45:58.043 --> 00:45:59.574
Kellie and I used to fight.


00:45:59.641 --> 00:46:01.745
But through the Noble work Dr.
Olsen is doing,


00:46:01.814 --> 00:46:03.744
We learned how to get along.


00:46:03.817 --> 00:46:05.986
Besides, once the merge happens,


00:46:06.048 --> 00:46:07.588
Everything will feel right to you.


00:46:07.659 --> 00:46:10.690
The merge?
I like where this is going.


00:46:10.758 --> 00:46:14.132
Not with me, silly.
With Cody.


00:46:15.564 --> 00:46:17.532
And I just threw up
in my mouth a little bit.


00:46:17.606 --> 00:46:19.678
Zack, your brother needs you.


00:46:19.736 --> 00:46:21.477
Cody doesn't need anyone but Cody.


00:46:21.545 --> 00:46:25.719
You're wrong. You'll see.
The merge will fix everything.


00:46:25.778 --> 00:46:28.822
Cody needs you here.
We all need you here.


00:46:28.893 --> 00:46:30.093
Please, Zack?


00:46:49.283 --> 00:46:51.326
She's never gonna forgive me.


00:47:08.387 --> 00:47:10.786
I'm sorry, Cody,


00:47:10.860 --> 00:47:14.262
But without Zack, you're of no use to me.


00:47:14.331 --> 00:47:16.865
But, Dr.
Olsen, can you just... No.


00:47:16.934 --> 00:47:20.333
Fine.
I'll do the next stage.


