No.


01:01:24.804 --> 01:01:26.046
No.


01:01:26.108 --> 01:01:28.443
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:28.513 --> 01:01:31.840
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:31.911 --> 01:01:33.237
Get Zack and Cody!
Zip line!


01:01:33.310 --> 01:01:35.875
That didn't work so well the last time.


01:01:35.944 --> 01:01:39.844
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:39.913 --> 01:01:43.881
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:43.940 --> 01:01:46.678
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:46.746 --> 01:01:49.475
Just keep them off the platform.
Hurry.


01:01:49.543 --> 01:01:51.813
I don't know how long I can hold them off.


01:01:51.879 --> 01:01:55.409
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:01:58.915 --> 01:02:00.115
Zack, helmet.
Helmet.


01:02:00.174 --> 01:02:02.242
Why?
Zip line regulations.


01:02:02.315 --> 01:02:04.140
Get back!
Get back!


01:02:05.409 --> 01:02:06.409
I said stay back!


01:02:09.818 --> 01:02:11.145
It's just out of my reach.


01:02:11.215 --> 01:02:13.642
Stay!


01:02:13.715 --> 01:02:16.711
Okay, on the count of three,
you jump up and grab on.


01:02:16.778 --> 01:02:17.980
Okay.


01:02:18.048 --> 01:02:19.878
Three, three, three!
Three, three, three!


01:02:20.477 --> 01:02:21.845
Zack!


01:02:21.916 --> 01:02:22.944
Get Zack and Cody!


01:02:23.014 --> 01:02:25.611
Zack!
Zack!


01:02:26.213 --> 01:02:27.355
Zack!


01:02:30.547 --> 01:02:32.444
We did it!


01:02:34.853 --> 01:02:36.081
That was awesome.


01:02:37.185 --> 01:02:39.680
Just hold on.
No, no, no, no.


01:02:42.286 --> 01:02:44.243
Yeah!


01:02:47.923 --> 01:02:49.721
That put some hair on my chest.


01:02:54.287 --> 01:02:56.114
Get Zack and Cody!


01:02:56.186 --> 01:02:58.185
And now the hair's gone.


01:02:58.258 --> 01:02:59.881
Let's hide in there!


01:02:59.954 --> 01:03:03.949
Oh, yeah, yeah. Let's hide in the
creepy, old, abandoned sawmill.


01:03:04.017 --> 01:03:06.820
That's safe. Why don't we bring
some toddlers in there with us?


01:03:09.853 --> 01:03:11.154
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:17.016 --> 01:03:19.526
Okay, I think we're safe here.


01:03:21.622 --> 01:03:22.924
Or not.


01:03:24.292 --> 01:03:25.923
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:27.957 --> 01:03:29.757
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:29.826 --> 01:03:31.226
Quick!
Climb up that ladder!


01:03:31.298 --> 01:03:32.997
Oh, that looks Rusty!


01:03:33.055 --> 01:03:35.558
I should've got my monthly tetanus shot.


01:03:35.620 --> 01:03:37.789
Dirty ladders are the least
of our problems right now.


01:03:37.859 --> 01:03:39.488
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:41.328 --> 01:03:43.295
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:44.894 --> 01:03:46.693
Get Zack and Cody!


01:03:50.330 --> 01:03:52.898
Blades! Why is it
always blades?


01:04:04.397 --> 01:04:06.595
Where's blankie when I need him?


01:04:12.161 --> 01:04:13.998
Get Zack and Cody!


01:04:16.067 --> 01:04:17.828
Get Zack and Cody!


01:04:19.364 --> 01:04:21.063
Get Zack and Cody!


01:04:21.133 --> 01:04:22.830
Run, run, run, run, run, run, run, run!


01:04:24.069 --> 01:04:25.070
Go, go!


01:04:29.394 --> 01:04:30.394
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


01:04:42.236 --> 01:04:43.232
Brother, hide in the trees!


01:04:45.969 --> 01:04:47.601
Okay.
What's happening?


01:04:47.669 --> 01:04:49.798
We're never going to outrun
those more athletic twins.


01:04:49.867 --> 01:04:51.066
We don't have to outrun them.


01:04:51.133 --> 01:04:52.401
I just have to outrun you.


01:04:53.834 --> 01:04:55.471
If I perish from heat exhaustion,


01:04:55.532 --> 01:04:57.429
Bury me in a stone tomb, standing up.


01:04:57.503 --> 01:04:59.001
With a piece of broken gold.


01:04:59.071 --> 01:05:01.137
Shh, I think I hear something!


01:05:01.204 --> 01:05:04.163
Tell Bailey that I respect her as a woman.


01:05:04.234 --> 01:05:05.775
No.
Okay.


01:05:07.068 --> 01:05:08.402
I think we're safe.


01:05:15.035 --> 01:05:16.636
Get Zack and Cody!


01:05:20.203 --> 01:05:21.870
Get Zack and Cody!


01:05:32.873 --> 01:05:33.968
Climb, climb!


01:05:49.877 --> 01:05:51.644
Get Zack and Cody!


01:06:09.507 --> 01:06:11.109
Okay. Question.


01:06:11.719 --> 01:06:13.014
Do you think it's as far down as it looks?


01:06:13.617 --> 01:06:15.284
It looks
like middle-earth.


01:06:17.482 --> 01:06:21.548
Zack, I want you to know
if our bones get crushed.


01:06:22.349 --> 01:06:25.715
Like cheap test tubes,
which is very likely,


01:06:26.317 --> 01:06:27.913
I just want you to know that...


01:06:28.582 --> 01:06:30.911
Yeah. Me, too.


01:06:34.548 --> 01:06:35.584
Okay. On three.


01:06:35.946 --> 01:06:37.714
One, two...


01:06:46.448 --> 01:06:49.253
I landed on my tummy.


01:06:51.318 --> 01:06:52.879
Are you okay?


01:06:52.951 --> 01:06:54.977
Yeah. Let's see.


01:06:55.050 --> 01:06:59.755
Leg. Knee. Ribs.


01:06:59.814 --> 01:07:03.520
Not sure what that is.
Yeah, I'm all right.


01:07:03.584 --> 01:07:05.489
We did it, Zack.
We made it!


01:07:10.926 --> 01:07:14.851
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:07:14.921 --> 01:07:18.815
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:07:18.888 --> 01:07:21.853
Get Zack and Cody!
Get Zack and Cody!


01:07:21.925 --> 01:07:23.122
Or not.


01:07:29.459 --> 01:07:32.057
Oh, good.
You're awake.


01:07:32.126 --> 01:07:33.754
Oh, good.
You're an evil idiot.


01:07:33.829 --> 01:07:36.552
Right. I'm an idiot, you're the
one that's locked down and wired.


01:07:36.623 --> 01:07:38.558
He's got a good point.


01:07:38.623 --> 01:07:41.558
Cody, why are we strapped down to
the mind transference facilitator?


01:07:41.626 --> 01:07:44.356
Because once I push this button,


01:07:44.424 --> 01:07:47.893
The electrons in your brains are
gonna violently smash together,


01:07:47.962 --> 01:07:50.819
And merge into one brain.


01:07:50.889 --> 01:07:52.290
That sounds like it's really going to hurt.


01:07:52.959 --> 01:07:54.058
Yes.


01:07:58.192 --> 01:07:59.624
Where are they?
There they are!


01:07:59.693 --> 01:08:01.291
Let them go!
Stay back!


01:08:03.058 --> 01:08:04.586
Careful! Nobody move.


01:08:05.856 --> 01:08:07.054
Cody!
Bailey!


01:08:07.127 --> 01:08:08.128
Woody!
Zack!


01:08:08.193 --> 01:08:09.366
London!


01:08:14.858 --> 01:08:16.229
Woody.
, son...


01:08:16.299 --> 01:08:18.628
Woody, what are you...
No, no, don't...


01:08:22.163 --> 01:08:23.960
Dang it.


01:08:24.032 --> 01:08:27.232
There's an electrical force field
surrounding the perimeter of the platform.


01:08:27.569 --> 01:08:28.868
Duh.


01:08:28.923 --> 01:08:31.393
Perfect timing,
Dr. Spaulding.


01:08:31.462 --> 01:08:33.966
We meet once again,
Dr. Olsen.


01:08:34.034 --> 01:08:36.700
I'm going to disintegrate
your individual minds now.


01:08:38.670 --> 01:08:42.234
Ronald, before you merge them,


01:08:42.294 --> 01:08:44.262
Why don't you show them who you really are?


01:09:04.937 --> 01:09:07.962
Wow, that is a pretty
intense chemical peel.


01:09:08.031 --> 01:09:09.734
I had a feeling
this guy was two-faced!


01:09:09.802 --> 01:09:13.599
Meet Ronald spaulding, my evil twin brother.


01:09:13.668 --> 01:09:15.267
Who disappeared two years ago.


01:09:15.337 --> 01:09:18.165
When the scientific
community threw him out.


01:09:18.235 --> 01:09:21.668
But I was here the whole time, waiting,


01:09:21.742 --> 01:09:23.669
Developing my brilliant plan.


01:09:23.739 --> 01:09:25.167
But if you're also a twin.


01:09:25.239 --> 01:09:28.007
Then why would you want
all twins to think alike?


01:09:28.074 --> 01:09:31.804
So no one would ever have to suffer
the pain that I did as a twin.


01:09:31.871 --> 01:09:35.309
Him, getting all the awards.
Him, the brilliant one.


01:09:35.371 --> 01:09:37.107
Him, the award winner.


01:09:37.168 --> 01:09:38.407
I feel you, brother.


01:09:38.474 --> 01:09:41.503
So you stole my work
to use for your own evil.


01:09:41.576 --> 01:09:43.243
I did.
But how?


01:09:43.305 --> 01:09:47.270
It was easy.
First, I posed as a janitor.


01:09:47.339 --> 01:09:49.679
Where I methodically stole your data.


01:09:49.738 --> 01:09:51.635
I designed this entire facility myself.


01:09:51.706 --> 01:09:54.604
It's completely state of
the art and wicked cool!


01:09:56.041 --> 01:09:58.070
Well, that looks promising.


01:10:10.339 --> 01:10:13.147
When I read Cody's paper on twins,


01:10:13.207 --> 01:10:16.544
I thought he and his brother
would be a great asset.


01:10:16.613 --> 01:10:19.681
So I went to the boat and I spied on them.


01:10:19.743 --> 01:10:22.577
I am so excited.
I've been planning our trip for a month.


01:10:22.651 --> 01:10:24.104
Whoa, whoa! Hey!


01:10:24.176 --> 01:10:25.944
That's what was in the letter!


01:10:26.013 --> 01:10:27.443
Why did you drop it, then?


01:10:27.514 --> 01:10:28.744
Hey! Hey, hey!


01:10:37.273 --> 01:10:39.979
I knew if I could lure them here,


01:10:40.043 --> 01:10:43.351
I could use them in my research.


01:10:43.408 --> 01:10:48.278
<i>Then all of my years of pain
would finally have a purpose.</i>


01:10:48.346 --> 01:10:53.313
I could create a controlled,
peaceful society!


01:10:53.379 --> 01:10:54.409
Through violence?


01:10:54.481 --> 01:10:56.248
Well, no plan is perfect!


01:10:56.318 --> 01:10:57.617
Can I just say something?


01:10:57.690 --> 01:10:59.846
Someone had a big bowl
of grumpy this morning.


01:11:55.758 --> 01:11:59.556
The merge is happening!


01:11:59.627 --> 01:12:03.421
You know, we should merge into my brain.
I have the superior intellect.


01:12:03.491 --> 01:12:05.827
You also have the inferior personality.


01:12:05.889 --> 01:12:07.327
I'd rather merge with a rock.


01:12:10.726 --> 01:12:13.163
Stop fighting!
You're ruining everything!


01:12:13.221 --> 01:12:15.160
- Stop it!
- You stop it!


01:12:18.954 --> 01:12:20.724
You know I told you
to get your head checked.


01:12:20.794 --> 01:12:22.892
But I'm sure the results
would come back as empty.


01:12:22.965 --> 01:12:24.424
My brain, my brain!


01:12:24.492 --> 01:12:26.634
No! No, wait!


01:12:26.692 --> 01:12:29.927
Your brain is all boring.
All you ever do is think.


01:12:29.995 --> 01:12:33.466
That's not true.
I also spend an inordinate amount of time.


01:12:33.524 --> 01:12:35.433
Worrying about global warming.


01:12:35.492 --> 01:12:39.058
And looking at things in my
closet that need to be pressed.


01:12:39.129 --> 01:12:41.097
Thanks for proving my point.
We're going into my brain.


01:12:47.361 --> 01:12:50.558
Zack...
I'm tired, Zack.


01:12:52.229 --> 01:12:56.237
Cody. If you can hear me,
keep fighting with Zack.


01:12:56.294 --> 01:12:59.000
By fighting, they're creating a
resistance and a power surge.


01:12:59.060 --> 01:13:00.500
To the machine that wants to merge them.


01:13:00.561 --> 01:13:02.727
It's as if the thing they do best, arguing,


01:13:02.796 --> 01:13:05.236
Is the one thing that can save them.


01:13:05.297 --> 01:13:06.895
I shop really well.
Can we use that?


01:13:10.501 --> 01:13:14.131
No, I can't go into your brain!


01:13:14.200 --> 01:13:16.299
You never use your brain.
How do we know it works?


01:13:20.606 --> 01:13:24.171
Well, at least it's not
jam-packed with stupid facts.


01:13:24.241 --> 01:13:25.899
And math thingies with numbers and letters.


01:13:25.966 --> 01:13:27.238
You mean equations?


01:13:27.299 --> 01:13:29.439
Stop!
You'll destroy everything.


01:13:29.505 --> 01:13:31.903
You know, I can't spend the rest
of my life in the head of someone.


01:13:31.973 --> 01:13:33.630
Who orders Sushi
well-done.


01:13:33.705 --> 01:13:35.603
Hey, Bailey, where'd you
get your hair done?


01:13:35.668 --> 01:13:37.241
At the groomer's?


01:13:37.301 --> 01:13:39.439
London! What?
I thought we're all joining in.


01:13:39.508 --> 01:13:42.575
One, the number of people who find
you interesting. Including yourself.


01:13:42.635 --> 01:13:45.344
Give in to the merge!
Give in!


01:13:45.405 --> 01:13:47.770
Well, I may not be interesting,
but at least I have a car!


01:13:54.745 --> 01:13:57.942
No!


01:14:02.340 --> 01:14:03.935
No! No!


01:14:14.644 --> 01:14:15.646
No!


01:14:21.609 --> 01:14:22.608
No!


01:14:30.982 --> 01:14:32.181
Come here, give me a hug!


01:14:35.082 --> 01:14:36.077
Ooh!


01:14:38.848 --> 01:14:41.612
You've ruined all my work.


01:14:43.280 --> 01:14:45.509
Now, you'll all pay the consequences!


01:14:45.582 --> 01:14:47.278
I'll merge all your minds!


01:14:47.349 --> 01:14:49.942
Wow, you really are a fruit basket.


01:14:51.283 --> 01:14:53.714
Fruit! Zack, fruit!


01:14:54.410 --> 01:14:55.809
But I'm not hungry.


01:14:56.480 --> 01:14:58.408
Got it!


01:14:58.478 --> 01:15:00.974
Bailey.
See that rope on the ground?


01:15:01.045 --> 01:15:02.216
Yeah. Mmm-hmm.


01:15:02.284 --> 01:15:04.012
Here's what I need you to do.


01:15:04.084 --> 01:15:06.280
Come on! Full power!


01:15:09.750 --> 01:15:10.846
Now!


01:15:11.486 --> 01:15:13.215
Yee-haw!


01:15:13.286 --> 01:15:14.883
Get along, little crazy scientist.


01:15:18.050 --> 01:15:19.421
Time!


01:15:19.483 --> 01:15:20.779
Let me go!
No.


01:15:20.849 --> 01:15:22.118
I will destroy all of you!


01:15:22.188 --> 01:15:23.618
Cody.


01:15:23.685 --> 01:15:25.754
Let me go!


01:15:25.813 --> 01:15:28.252
Dr. Spaulding, eat this, and think
good thoughts about your brother.


01:15:30.080 --> 01:15:31.349
Chew it.


01:15:36.316 --> 01:15:38.623
Donald? Really?


01:15:39.578 --> 01:15:41.382
You were always jealous of me?


01:15:42.048 --> 01:15:43.350
But you had everything.


01:15:43.420 --> 01:15:45.983
True.
But that's all I knew.


01:15:46.058 --> 01:15:49.323
I didn't know how to have fun like you did.


01:15:49.383 --> 01:15:53.291
So, all those years that I
was wishing I could be you,


01:15:53.349 --> 01:15:55.418
You were wishing you could be me?


01:15:55.490 --> 01:15:59.885
More than that.
I was wishing that we were us.


01:16:02.191 --> 01:16:04.821
Ah! Boys,
are you all right?


01:16:04.890 --> 01:16:05.891
We're fine, Mr. Moseby.


01:16:05.961 --> 01:16:07.690
Oh! Thank goodness.


01:16:07.760 --> 01:16:10.085
One more minute and our
personalities would have been gone.


01:16:10.156 --> 01:16:12.796
The one time I get a parking
spot right out front!


01:16:13.156 --> 01:16:14.690
Donald.


01:16:14.762 --> 01:16:17.928
I was wrong the whole time.
I'm sorry.


01:16:17.999 --> 01:16:20.096
I forgive you, Ronald.


01:16:20.169 --> 01:16:22.992
When I get out of prison, let's have lunch.


01:16:23.066 --> 01:16:24.492
I'll be here. Waiting.


01:16:25.563 --> 01:16:29.299
I'll be 143, and hungry, but waiting.


01:16:29.372 --> 01:16:30.627
Okay. No fruit.


01:16:30.698 --> 01:16:32.839
No fruit.
Fruity tale.


01:16:39.931 --> 01:16:42.097
You know, they make you
guys seem almost normal.


01:16:44.667 --> 01:16:46.134
That was fun.
Want to go shopping?


01:16:46.205 --> 01:16:47.264
No. No shopping.


01:16:47.335 --> 01:16:49.234
How about a sandwich?


01:16:52.037 --> 01:16:55.136
See what we can accomplish
when we work together?


01:16:55.205 --> 01:16:58.333
You know, we make a pretty good team.


01:17:11.204 --> 01:17:13.171
Okay, this was the best spring break ever,


01:17:13.246 --> 01:17:14.969
and we managed to do everything on my list,


01:17:15.040 --> 01:17:17.668
including the museum
of microscopic magnets.


01:17:17.738 --> 01:17:19.438
What was your favorite?


01:17:19.507 --> 01:17:22.742
Well, it's a toss up between the
Erosional Granite Sandstone Sea Cave,


01:17:22.800 --> 01:17:24.799
and that giant ball of twine.


01:17:49.579 --> 01:17:52.979
"Do not park.
Zack Martin exempted."


01:17:53.046 --> 01:17:54.904
Perfect.
Sweet ride!


01:17:54.973 --> 01:17:56.245
Hey!


01:17:57.713 --> 01:18:00.638
Thanks for the car.
Isn't she pretty?


01:18:03.349 --> 01:18:04.706
No. No, no.
Zack, Zack!


01:18:08.514 --> 01:18:09.679
Oh, no!


01:18:14.976 --> 01:18:17.377
Ooh, goody!
My summer wardrobe's here!


01:18:19.316 --> 01:18:21.912
Well, spring break's over.


01:18:21.982 --> 01:18:24.506
Now, If I could just make
it to summer vacation.

